  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "All night their road lay through the defiles, and at dawn the peaks lit up one after another.",
      "shot": 0,
      "at": 0.25,
      "seconds": 5.7
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "They were a day ahead of the Avenging Angels, and Hope drove them on without mercy.",
      "shot": 1,
      "at": 7.458,
      "seconds": 6.26
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A great rock came thundering down and woke the echoes, and the weary horses broke into a gallop.",
      "shot": 2,
      "at": 14.75,
      "seconds": 6.2
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "They will be upon our track by now. Everything depends on speed.",
      "shot": 3,
      "at": 21.958,
      "seconds": 4.53
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "On the second day the food ran out, so Hope made a fire in a sheltered nook.",
      "shot": 4,
      "at": 28.0,
      "seconds": 5.61
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He shouldered his rifle, and went off after whatever the mountains might give him.",
      "shot": 5,
      "at": 34.625,
      "seconds": 4.92
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He looked back once: the old man and the girl bent to the fire, the animals behind them.",
      "shot": 6,
      "at": 40.583,
      "seconds": 5.58
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Three hours brought him a big-horn on a pinnacle, and one long steady shot brought it down.",
      "shot": 7,
      "at": 47.5,
      "seconds": 6.3
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "With a haunch over his shoulder he turned back, and lost his way among the gorges till dark.",
      "shot": 8,
      "at": 54.833,
      "seconds": 6.12
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "At the mouth of the defile he put his hands to his mouth and hallooed. Nothing came back.",
      "shot": 9,
      "at": 61.958,
      "seconds": 5.82
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The fire had burned to a pile of ashes, and no one had tended it since he left.",
      "shot": 11,
      "at": 71.5,
      "seconds": 5.54
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The ground was stamped by hooves, and to one side lay a heap of red soil, fresh dug.",
      "shot": 12,
      "at": 78.042,
      "seconds": 6.2
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A stick stood in it, with a paper: John Ferrier, of Salt Lake City. Died August the fourth.",
      "shot": 13,
      "at": 85.25,
      "seconds": 6.62
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "Then I have one thing left.",
      "shot": 14,
      "at": 93.208,
      "seconds": 1.82
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He cooked what would last him, and walked back through the mountains on the track of the Angels.",
      "shot": 15,
      "at": 96.833,
      "seconds": 5.5
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "On the sixth day he stood above the city again, and there were flags in the streets.",
      "shot": 16,
      "at": 103.667,
      "seconds": 4.98
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A rider came up the canyon, a Mormon named Cowper, who owed him a kindness or two.",
      "shot": 17,
      "at": 110.083,
      "seconds": 5.86
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "cowper",
      "text": "You are mad to come here. There is a warrant out against you, from the Holy Four.",
      "shot": 18,
      "at": 116.958,
      "seconds": 5.12
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "jefferson_hope",
      "text": "What has become of Lucy Ferrier?",
      "shot": 19,
      "at": 123.083,
      "seconds": 2.79
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "cowper",
      "text": "Married yesterday, to young Drebber. Hold up, man, hold up.",
      "shot": 20,
      "at": 126.875,
      "seconds": 4.48
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "cowper",
      "text": "Stangerson shot her father. And I saw death in her face yesterday.",
      "shot": 22,
      "at": 135.083,
      "seconds": 4.36
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "She never held up her head again, and died within the month; the wives sat up with her.",
      "shot": 23,
      "at": 141.25,
      "seconds": 5.61
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "In the grey of the morning the door was flung open on a wild weather-beaten man.",
      "shot": 24,
      "at": 147.875,
      "seconds": 4.96
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He kissed the cold forehead, and took the wedding ring from her finger.",
      "shot": 25,
      "at": 153.875,
      "seconds": 4.22
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "drebber_wife",
      "text": "The ring is gone.",
      "shot": 26,
      "at": 159.625,
      "seconds": 1.67
    }
  ]
}